{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106532","id":2526222304,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6Wkxfg","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106532","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106532.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106532.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106532","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106532/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106532/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106532/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/31610b058bf17eb3db510632d2e708701a5cccfc","number":106532,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix texture atlas import deadlock by keeping `group_file=` on failed `import_file()` attempts","user":{"login":"isaaccp","id":8712,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8712?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/isaaccp","html_url":"https://github.com/isaaccp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isaaccp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isaaccp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isaaccp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isaaccp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isaaccp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isaaccp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isaaccp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isaaccp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isaaccp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The problem is that when a texture_atlas resource is loaded during startup (e.g. because it's referenced by an autoload) using _load_resource_on_startup(), we always call _reimport_file() even if the resource has a group_file= attribute.\r\n\r\nThis causes _reimport_file() to drop the group_file= and when reimport_files() is called later it causes the deadlock as detailed below and in the issue linked.\r\n\r\nI was wondering whether we could try to instead update _load_resource_on_startup() so it's aware of group_file, but at that point the filesystem hasn't been scanned yet, so it doesn't seem possible to find all the files in the group.\r\n\r\nInstead, this PR makes it so _reimport_file() doesn't drop the group_file= attribute when import fails during startup. This allows the file to be loaded as part of the group in reimport_files().\r\n\r\nWithout group_file= set, this actually causes a deadlock in the editor as the ResourceImporterTextureAtlas::import() call attempts to use the rendering server while the main thread is waiting on a semaphore for imports to finish.\r\n\r\nThis fixes #104796 (verified locally), which has more details about the issue.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":890310502,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4OTAzMTA1MDI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:import","name":"topic:import","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12939969,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AxXLB","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/23","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/23","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/23/labels","number":23,"state":"closed","title":"4.6","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_u